tical to a host-mode run, which proves host and pod parity;\n  - otherwise, check structure only: 3 findings, A's two files, and the `^trufflehog:[0-9a-f]{16}$` format;\n  - no planted value in stdout, stderr or `hostTmp`;\n  - a second run is identical.\n\n**Step 3: docs.**\n\n`docs/proposal.md`. #215 covers `route`, the label-table note and the pre-filing guard, and #216 covers the Scanners table row, the starter list and the Configuration line. Add only what is missing, and make sure the \"The trufflehog scanner\" paragraph covers:\n- the mode: HEAD only, no history, with a history scanner as a follow-up (#224);\n- the flags `--no-verification`, `--no-update`, `--no-ignore-tag`, `--fail-on-scan-errors`, and that the forbidden flags are never passed;\n- the allowlist projection: only the detector, `file:line` and a fingerprint ever leave the scan (public issues show `file:line`);\n- the fingerprint scheme, and that the hash is unsalted, an offline oracle for a low-entropy value that is already in the repo at HEAD, accepted;\n- **gone from HEAD is not revoked**: autoclose closes as completed, and the body tells the human to rotate first;\n- the backpressure caveat: at `max_open` the scanner is skipped, so new leaks go unseen until a human resolves one (scanner failure streaks are posted on the status issue, #221);\n- any future \"commit scanner logs\" change must exclude this scanner;\n- that on a public repo with GitHub secret scanning off this scanner is the only detection channel and cannot stop a push;\n- the licence: TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0, kept out of the published `ard` image; the binary comes from the role's Dockerfile or a host install.\n\n`CLAUDE.md`: on line 54 (`internal/roles/`), add `scanners/trufflehog` to the starter list if #216 has not. Leave line 74 alone.\n\n**Error behaviour.** Only tests and docs change. The integration tests fail and never skip once `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN` is set (a version mismatch fails); the Docker test skips only when Docker