{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLgKPhvScigAWWRo74UB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019frmXwRCQsb6DFyDPoJR6U","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"`commit` is the scanned SHA, recorded in `.ard/<n>/issue.md`; history is not scanned. TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0: it is installed by the role's Dockerfile and is not in the published `ard` image.\"\nassert old in s\nnew=\"`commit` is the scanned SHA, recorded in `.ard/<n>/issue.md`; only HEAD is scanned, and a history scanner is a follow-up (#224). The forbidden flags (`--since-commit`, `--max-depth`, `--detector-timeout`, `--archive-timeout`, `--filter-unverified`, `--filter-entropy`, `--results`) are never passed, because a partial or load-dependent result would autoclose live findings. Caveats: (1) a secret gone from HEAD is not revoked; autoclose closes the issue as completed, so the issue body tells the human to rotate first. (2) The fingerprint hash is unsalted, an offline oracle for a low-entropy value that is already in the repo at HEAD; accepted. (3) Issues on a public repo show `file:line`. (4) At `max_open` the scanner is skipped, so new leaks go unseen until a human resolves one; scanner failure streaks are posted on the status issue (#221). (5) Any future change that commits scanner logs must exclude this scanner. (6) On a public repo with GitHub secret scanning off, this scanner is the only detection channel, and it cannot stop a push. TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0: it is installed by the role's Dockerfile (or a host install) and is not in the published `ard` image or the root `Dockerfile`. Host and Docker integration tests (`go test -tags integration -run Trufflehog ./internal/roles/`, with `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN` at the Dockerfile's pinned version) prove the role against a real binary and image.\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\nmake lint test 2>&1 | tail -8; git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_read_input_tokens":38901,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":449},"output_tokens":60,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"674570e0-cf8a-493c-8777-d3d2c16c66e6","uuid":"216f7174-cbc1-4cb5-b986-7119b23240d6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:51:18.729Z","request_id":"req_011ChLgKPZyyo1FjiMuwQVCb"}
